{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1391186-how-do-you-successfully-run-the-tremere-in-v5","id":1391186,"title":"How do You successfully run the Tremere in V5?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-24T06:56:32-07:00","id":1391186,"title":"How do You successfully run the Tremere in V5?","content":"I would like to hear <b>your </b>examples of how you have <b>successfully </b>integrated the Tremere Clan into your V5 chronicles. My question is specifically about the clan as a group in <b>your city.</b> How to they work, how do you present them to the players. <br /> <br /> I have not been happy with my attempts with the new material and would be happy to purchase a dot of <b>malwa</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26030-mfalkenb","name":"mfalkenb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T07:13:31-07:00","id":1391189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mfalkenb</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1391186-how-do-you-successfully-run-the-tremere-in-v5#post1391186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to hear <b>your </b>examples of how you have <b>successfully </b>integrated the Tremere Clan into your V5 chronicles. My question is specifically about the clan as a group in <b>your city.</b> How to they work, how do you present them to the players.<br /> <br /> I have not been happy with my attempts with the new material and would be happy to purchase a dot of <b>malwa</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Jacksonville, Florida by Night</b><br /> <br /> In my home game, <b>Karl Barric</b> was the Regent of the city's Tremere and one of the most nastiest pieces of work you'll find among the Pyramid. He controlled the local meth trade, sold human slaves, and was a power-player in the city due to his monopoly on Blood Sorcery with the Sabbat just a stone's throw away in Miami. The death of the Council of Seven resulted in one of the player characters, <b>Synnara</b>, to use the help of the PCs to create her own chantry of <b>House Carna</b> where she opened it up as a refuge for Tremere oppressed and abused by the Pyramid. Karl planned to annihilate them but the player characters and the support of the Prince resulted in them receiving legitimacy due to helping push back the Sabbat siege of 2019.<br /> <br /> Karl Barric's chantry is a traditionalist House Tremere chantry that answers (theoretically) to <b>Karl Schrekt</b> back in <b>Prague</b> (he isn't going anywhere near Vienna). Karl has a lot more freedom than he did under the old Pyramid but pretends that every action he takes is done with the full support of the Clan. In place of Blood Bonds, he forces those apprentices under his command to sign <b>Blood Contracts</b> and also give him phylactery of their blood that will allow him to kill them if they disobey him. The fact this puts him at odds with the Prince of the City is something that heasn't been tested...yet.<br /> <br /> Synnara, by contrast, is attempting to build up the power of the Tremere in the city by offering freedom to those who are willing to join her coven with the premise of sharing freely knowledge as well as having a brotherhood/sisterhood rather than a hierarchy. This is running into problems because quite a few Tremere are mistaking her attempts at mutually beneficial alliance for weakness. Most of her chantry is new apprentices fearing their old masters or who have screwed up plus a couple of Elders who just want a stable place to work.<br /> <br /> The two sides are obviously feuding but doing so under the table as the Prince has come very close to killing Saul several times and he doesn't have anywhere to run to despite his power. He can't even kill the Prince because her position was guaranteed by a Justicar during the Sabbat siege and the rest of the Primogen loathe him.<br /> <br /> Recently, a trio of <b>House Ipsissimus</b> hackers have moved in with no interest in joining either of the chantries but actively interested in joining the local Anarchs in fighting against the Camarilla as well as Second Inquisition. Karl is debating a plan to work with Synnara to destroy this group because as much as he loathes her, he doesn't want to divide the power of the Tremere further.<br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> I'm happy to discuss how else I view V5's Tremere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-24-2020, 10:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T09:22:17-07:00","id":1391201,"title":"","content":"The other houses are a ploy. They all answer to the inner circle and Tremere. <br /> <br /> So why the split? <br /> <br /> <b>First off</b>, the Tremere have a massive image problem, and the clan has been a victim of it's own success. They're too organized, they make too much money, they're too good at competing for influence; Thaumaturgy is too profitable and the gap between people owing the Tremere and the Tremere owing people is simply <i>huge</i>. They pissed off the Tzmisce, Gangrel and Nosferatu in their inception, They may have upset the malks in eating the sau's, they later took a big dump on the assamites, their expanding wealth and influence has troubled their greatest allies, the Ventrue, and they're too much &quot;The Man&quot; for Brujah. Even with a few good &quot;faces&quot; of the clan, the group as a whole has always had a sinister reputation and it's well known that they will put the pyramid before a personal friendship, so nobody gets close. Instead more vampires are worried that the warlocks are secretly after samples of your blood for nefarious rituals. It doesn't help at all that, like shitty villains in chinese comics, the Tremere have a tendancy to brandish the name of their clan in a &quot;You can't afford to fuck with me&quot; kinda way. Also, the Tremere tend to attract powergamers that lack social skills.... Am i allowed to say that ? <i>That guy</i> often picks Tremere, and he or she'll reinforce everything you've heard about the clan. <br /> <br /> In short, the Tremere are like a kid at school that gets great grades all the time and rubs it in the face of everyone who didn't get good grades. Unlike the rich kid in the class that everybody likes (Ventrue) who has a sense of decorum, Tremere displays his wealth with the worst possible taste; A golden Iphone, a flash car, an exotic pet gargoyle... you get the picture. In actuality, most Tremere are smart people who don't do this; but the ones who do ruin it for the rest of them. <br /> <br /> <br /> So, we get to V5. <br /> Ipsimus is just a licence to have Tremere chantries in anarch territory. They, on the sly, knock off rival bloodmages in order to ensure the Tremere monopoly on Thaumaturgy. Goratrix is the same. <br /> <br /> House Carna is basically House Tremere <i>Democrat edition</i>. They're the real image shifters here. It's the same right wing-economics but with some radical left wing social policies to give that illusion of being nice. The Tremere are a one-party state pretending to have different options. They're aggressively Pro-women, they'll use your prefered pronouns, they'll read tea-leaves and publicly display advocacy for gossip astrology, wicca and neopaganism, palm reading... all the while they teach hermetic theory in private. They'll exploit you, but instead of a man telling you to what to do, a woman will give you &quot;Guidance&quot;. They're the same fucking people, they've just gotten a makeover. They read more like what an old person thinks millennials would like, less like what millennial would actually be interested in. Imagine men in their 40's writing childrens cartoons with &quot;cool&quot; stuff from 10 years ago. Now imagine those 40 year old men are vampires with centuries under their belt. <br /> <br /> House Carna and Tremere are like two dragons dancing in the sky. They look like they're fighting, but they're in love. Everyone's much happier that the big, bad, monolithic Tremere got knocked down a peg, ignorant that there's really just one big happy tremere family They can relax more. They can be more comfortable around Tremere. The elders are supposedly dead. The Tremere aren't a threat. If the Tremere are victims of their own success, then the appearance of failure can bring them together. <br /> <br /> <b>Second thing.</b><br /> I've said all this about the split of clan tremere being a cunning ploy for outsiders, but the lower down vampires don't really know anything about that (The advantages of a pyramid system). Anyone below the rank of Lord knows little or nothing. As such, with the clan weakness <i>Temporarily </i>inverted, the low ranking Tremere have plenty of opportunities to try jump ship. In some cases, this is arranged for by the pyramid, but in other cases, this is a genuine defector. The Tremere are using this oppertunity to purge disloyal fools they've mistakenly embraced. With great irony, the arranged &quot;spies&quot; are declared brothers and sisters, and those who genuinely wanted to escape the pyramid for the ideals of Carna are declared spies and killed. A few tactical moves are sometimes forgiven by higher-ups and a few arranged spies are killed off because, y'know, vampires can be shitty. But ultimately the remaining Tremere are far more loyal to the pyramid than before, even if they don't know it and sometimes skirmish with those of other houses. <br /> <br /> <br /> So how to run Tremere now? The same, but with petty rivalries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T17:56:02-07:00","id":1391366,"title":"","content":"Because of its occulted nature, the Tremere chantry was the locus of the shadow Camarilla presence in Anarch Berlin, where one of the PCs ended up converting to the Camarilla cause. While House Ipsissimus was properly independent, being descended from the original Anarch Tremere, House Tremere and House Carna had reached an understanding and were effectively two different cultures within the clan working towards a common purpose. Basically, the core Tremere were finally forced to acknowledge that there is strength in diversity and decentralization, and Carna\u2019s followers were just happy to be able to do things their way without reprisal. To that end, the Camarilla houses (particularly House Carna) had seeded Camarilla-loyal advisors in the courts of the city\u2019s major barons, and they ended up being the sect\u2019s main source of information on Anarch activities, as well as subtle influence.<br /> <br /> Berlin\u2019s Camarilla was playing the long game, keeping individual Anarch baronies at odds and biding their time, recruiting promising members, and waiting for the opportunity to carve an autonomous zone for themselves within the city, then retake territory as the opportunity arose. Since they offered things no other clan could offer, the Tremere ended up being pretty well dug into Anarch domains, and thus were the main boots on the ground for the Camarilla\u2019s shadow conspiracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}